\label{lemma-zariski}
Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes and $U \subset S$ an open. If
\begin{enumerate}
\item $f$ is separated, locally of finite type, and flat,
\item $f^{-1}(U) \to U$ is an isomorphism, and
\item $U \subset S$ is retrocompact and scheme theoretically dense,
\end{enumerate}
then $f$ is an open immersion.

\label{lemma-etale-nbhd-dominates-smooth}
\begin{slogan}
Smooth morphisms admit \'etale local sections.
\end{slogan}
\begin{reference}
See \cite[Corollaire 17.16.3 (ii)]{EGA4}.
\end{reference}
Let $f : X \to S$ be a smooth morphism of schemes.
Let $s \in S$ be a point in the image of $f$.
Then there exists an \'etale neighbourhood $(S', s') \to (S, s)$
and a $S$-morphism $S' \to X$.

